1
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:08,500
A world light-years beyond your imagination.

2
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:11,000
Krull is a action, adventure, fantasy film directed by Peter Yates.

3
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:13,500
A prince and a fellowship of companions set out to rescue his bride from a
fortress of alien invaders who have arrived on their home planet.

4
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Prince Colwyn, played by Ken Marshall.

5
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:18,500
Lyssa, played by Lysette Anthony.

6
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:21,000
Ynyr, played by Freddie Jones.

7
00:35:17,500 --> 00:35:23,500
Widow of the Web, played by Francesca Annis.

8
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:26,000
Torquil, played by Alun Armstrong.

9
00:45:22,500 --> 00:45:28,500
Ergo, played by David Battley.

10
00:50:25,000 --> 00:50:31,000
Krull is a 1983 British science fantasy adventure film directed by
Peter Yates and distributed by Columbia Pictures.

11
00:55:27,500 --> 00:55:33,500
It stars Ken Marshall, Lysette Anthony, Freddie Jones,
Francesca Annis, David Battley and Alun Armstrong.

12
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Liam Neeson and Robbie Coltrane, still early in their
film careers, appear in supporting roles.

13
01:05:32,500 --> 01:05:38,500
The story follows Prince Colwyn (Marshall) and a fellowship of companions who set out to rescue his bride,
Princess Lyssa (Anthony), from a fortress of alien invaders who have arrived on their home planet.

14
01:10:35,000 --> 01:10:41,000
Development on the film began in 1980, when Columbia Pictures President Frank
Price gave producer Ron Silverman the idea to produce a fantasy film.

15
01:15:37,500 --> 01:15:43,500
Krull was shot in England at Pinewood Studios and
on-location in Italy and Spain.

16
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:46,000
Nick Maley designed the creature and prosthetic makeup effects seen in the film.

17
01:25:42,500 --> 01:25:48,500
The film score was composed by James Horner and
performed by the London Symphony Orchestra.

18
01:30:45,000 --> 01:30:51,000
Krull was released in the United States on July 29, 1983, and
in the United Kingdom later that December.

19
01:35:47,500 --> 01:35:53,500
The film was a box-office bomb upon release, and critical opinion
has been mixed, both upon release and in retrospect.

20
01:40:50,000 --> 01:40:56,000
Reviewers have highlighted its visual effects and soundtrack, while others
have criticized its plot as being derivative and nonsensical.

21
01:45:52,500 --> 01:45:58,500
In the years since its release, the film has developed a cult following.

22
01:50:55,000 --> 01:51:01,000
The film explores themes of kingdom, dead body,
magical object, fortress, swashbuckler.

23
01:55:57,500 --> 01:56:03,500
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
